WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.234
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online TOEIC preparation.

2
00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.909
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:17.736
Unit six: Part 3: Workplace Conversations. Today you will follow short business conversations and answer gist and detail questions.

4
00:00:18.036 --> 00:00:20.537
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.570
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.417 --> 00:00:26.534
Conversation.

7
00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:30.490
Conversation means a talk between two or three people.

8
00:00:31.083 --> 00:00:32.769
Listen to the conversation.

9
00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:35.978
Your turn. Say: Conversation.

10
00:00:38.833 --> 00:00:39.939
Conversation.

11
00:00:40.683 --> 00:00:41.452
Colleague.

12
00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.415
Colleague means a person you work with.

13
00:00:45.017 --> 00:00:46.447
She spoke to a colleague.

14
00:00:47.050 --> 00:00:49.273
Your turn. Say: Colleague.

15
00:00:52.133 --> 00:00:53.053
Colleague.

16
00:00:53.817 --> 00:00:54.632
Client.

17
00:00:55.617 --> 00:00:57.779
Client means a customer of a business.

18
00:00:58.383 --> 00:01:00.127
A client called this morning.

19
00:01:00.717 --> 00:01:03.230
Your turn. Say: Client.

20
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:07.056
Client.

21
00:01:07.817 --> 00:01:08.678
Order.

22
00:01:09.683 --> 00:01:11.869
Order means a request to buy goods.

23
00:01:12.483 --> 00:01:14.158
The order arrives on Monday.

24
00:01:14.750 --> 00:01:16.891
Your turn. Say: Order.

25
00:01:19.733 --> 00:01:20.595
Order.

26
00:01:21.350 --> 00:01:22.386
Invoice.

27
00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:25.963
Invoice means a bill for goods or services.

28
00:01:26.550 --> 00:01:28.015
Send the invoice today.

29
00:01:28.617 --> 00:01:31.188
Your turn. Say: Invoice.

30
00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:35.209
Invoice.

31
00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:36.939
Agenda.

32
00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:40.646
Agenda means a list of topics for a meeting.

33
00:01:41.250 --> 00:01:42.623
Check the agenda.

34
00:01:43.217 --> 00:01:46.415
Your turn. Say: Agenda.

35
00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.268
Agenda.

36
00:01:51.017 --> 00:01:51.855
Delay.

37
00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:55.209
Delay means a time when something is late.

38
00:01:55.817 --> 00:01:57.445
There is a delay in delivery.

39
00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.563
Your turn. Say: Delay.

40
00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.169
Delay.

41
00:02:04.917 --> 00:02:05.848
Arrange.

42
00:02:06.850 --> 00:02:09.244
Arrange means to plan or organise.

43
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:11.374
I'll arrange a taxi.

44
00:02:11.983 --> 00:02:14.473
Your turn. Say: Arrange.

45
00:02:17.333 --> 00:02:18.404
Arrange.

46
00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:23.129
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:23.983 --> 00:02:26.157
Visal, how does Part 3 work?

48
00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:37.495
You hear a conversation between two or three people and answer three questions about it. The conversations are about work topics such as orders, schedules and problems.

49
00:02:38.583 --> 00:02:40.989
What should I do before the audio starts?

50
00:02:42.083 --> 00:02:53.585
Read the three questions and the options quickly. Underline key words like who, why and what next. Then listen for the answers in the same order as the questions.

51
00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:56.486
What do questions often ask?

52
00:02:57.583 --> 00:03:10.638
They ask about the topic, the problem, the speaker's job and what will happen next. The final question often asks about the next action, so listen to the last lines carefully.

53
00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.231
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:14.083 --> 00:03:18.277
Grammar focus: Strategy: preview questions, then listen in order.

55
00:03:18.577 --> 00:03:19.741
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:22.670
The woman will send the invoice tomorrow.

57
00:03:23.583 --> 00:03:26.558
The delay is caused by a problem at the warehouse.

58
00:03:27.500 --> 00:03:35.528
Read the questions first, then listen for each answer in order. Pay special attention to the last lines, because they usually give the next step.

59
00:03:36.283 --> 00:03:40.596
Be careful! Don't say: I do not read the questions first.

60
00:03:42.533 --> 00:03:45.067
Say: I read the questions first.

61
00:03:45.367 --> 00:03:46.867
Preview the questions.

62
00:03:47.667 --> 00:03:50.389
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.329
A Delayed Order.

64
00:03:52.629 --> 00:03:55.209
Two colleagues discuss a client's order.

65
00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.734
The man says there is a delay at the warehouse.

66
00:03:59.733 --> 00:04:02.511
The woman suggests calling the client to explain.

67
00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:05.825
They agree to ship half of the order today.

68
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:09.146
The woman will send the new invoice tomorrow.

69
00:04:10.233 --> 00:04:14.398
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:15.250 --> 00:04:18.376
In Part 3 you answer blank questions per conversation.

71
00:04:18.676 --> 00:04:21.644
A, three. B, five. C, one.

72
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:26.909
The answer is A: three.

73
00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:30.479
You should read the questions blank the audio.

74
00:04:30.779 --> 00:04:34.026
A, never. B, before. C, after.

75
00:04:37.567 --> 00:04:39.473
The answer is B: before.

76
00:04:40.617 --> 00:04:42.024
What caused the delay?

77
00:04:42.324 --> 00:04:46.628
A, bad weather. B, a holiday. C, a warehouse problem.

78
00:04:50.167 --> 00:04:52.700
The answer is C: a warehouse problem.

79
00:04:53.850 --> 00:04:55.606
What will the woman do tomorrow?

80
00:04:55.906 --> 00:05:00.360
A, send an invoice. B, visit Paris. C, call the bank.

81
00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:06.201
The answer is A: send an invoice.

82
00:05:07.350 --> 00:05:10.104
The last question often asks about the blank.

83
00:05:10.404 --> 00:05:14.243
A, date of birth. B, next action. C, title.

84
00:05:17.800 --> 00:05:20.229
The answer is B: next action.

85
00:05:21.433 --> 00:05:24.655
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:25.517 --> 00:05:27.841
How do you answer Part 3 questions?

87
00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.150
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:38.450 --> 00:05:50.080
I read the three questions first and underline the key words. While I listen, I find the answers in the same order as the questions. I listen to the last lines for the next action.

89
00:05:50.380 --> 00:05:52.228
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:53.117 --> 00:05:59.484
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: preview questions, then listen in order.

91
00:05:59.784 --> 00:06:04.085
Today's value is preparedness. Get ready before an emergency happens.

92
00:06:04.385 --> 00:06:06.689
See you in Unit seven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:06.989 --> 00:06:09.816
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

